; canonical arrays: one half-and-half array reached from either default
; a starts all 0 and gets 5 at indices 0 and 1; b starts all 5 and
; gets 0 at indices 2 and 3; extensionally they are the same array
1 sort bitvec 2
2 sort bitvec 4
3 sort array 1 2
4 sort bitvec 1
5 zero 2
6 constd 2 5
7 state 3 a
8 init 3 7 5
9 state 3 b
10 init 3 9 6
11 constd 1 0
12 constd 1 1
13 constd 1 2
14 constd 1 3
15 write 3 7 11 6
16 write 3 15 12 6
17 write 3 9 13 5
18 write 3 17 14 5
19 eq 4 16 18
20 bad 19
